<title>UK: IEA supply/demand highlights - end June report.</title>
<headline>IEA supply/demand highlights - end June report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following table highlights the oil supply-demand and stock estimates included in the International Energy Agency's latest Monthly Oil Market Report. Figures in million barrels per day.</p>
<p>		  1995 1Q96 2Q96 3Q96 4Q96 1996 1Q97 2Q97 3Q97 4Q97 1997 1998</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p> OECD	   40.4 42.2 39.6 40.6 42.2 41.2 41.9 40.6 41.3 42.9 41.7 42.1</p>
<p> NON-OECD     29.9 31.0 30.3 30.4 31.5 30.8 32.0 31.9 31.5 33.1 32.1 33.5</p>
<p> TOTAL	  70.3 73.2 69.9 71.0 73.7 72.0 73.9 72.6 72.8 75.9 73.8 75.5</p>
<p>SUPPLY</p>
<p> NON-OPEC     42.4 43.4 43.4 43.5 44.4 43.7 44.4 44.5 45.1 46.7 45.2 47.2</p>
<p> OPEC CRUDE   25.1 25.7 25.6 25.9 26.2 25.9 26.9 26.8</p>
<p> OPEC NGLS     2.4  2.5  2.6  2.7  2.7  2.6  2.7  2.8  2.9  3.0  2.9  3.0</p>
<p> TOTAL OPEC   27.5 28.2 28.2 28.6 28.9 28.5 29.7</p>
<p> TOTAL SUPPLY 70.0 71.6 71.5 72.1 73.3 72.1 74.1 74.2</p>
<p> OPEC CALL*   25.4 27.3 24.0 24.9 26.7 25.7 26.8 25.6 24.6 26.2 25.7 25.3</p>
<p> IND STOCKS   -0.3 -1.8 +1.2 +0.4 -0.4 -0.1 +0.2 +0.6</p>
<p> TOT STCK BAL -0.3 -1.3 +1.1 +0.3 -0.5 +0.1 +0.1 +0.6</p>
<p> FSU NET EXP   2.4  2.4  2.8  2.8  2.9  2.7  2.7  2.79 2.9  2.7 2.8 2.9</p>
<p>* Implied call on OPEC crude equals total demand minus total non-OPEC supply minus OPEC NGLs. Thus includes &quot;miscellaneous to balance&quot; for historical time periods.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
